      "_evidence": "For the first regression, coach/teammate weight pressures and appearance pressures explained 13.5% (Adj [R.sup.2] =. 126, p < .001) of the variance in bulimic symptomology. The body image measures accounted for an additional 8.1% of the variance (p < .00 I), whereas the block of negative affect measures contributed a nonsignificant additional 3.5% of the variance. Self-esteem was entered last, and accounted for 3.0% of the variance (p = .005). The final model was significant, F (9.193) = 8.34, p < .001, and accounted for 28% (Adj [R.sup.2] = .246) of the BULIT-R variance. Specifically, more weight pressures from coaches and teammates ([beta] =. 156, p = .05) and lower self-esteem ([beta] = -.246, p < .01) were related to higher levels of bulimic symptomatology.",
